I think you're being unfair now.  Part of nethack's charm is that it's
so amazingly complex and that it, in a weird sense, is 'realistic'.
Not in the sense that it simulates real life (which probably would be boring,
anyway), but in that it simulates an imagined setting in a fantasy world.
I.e. you can drink from sinks, dip things in different fluids, etc. etc.
So i don't really think it would be non-nethackish if only male creatures
could lay eggs (But you could always assume that when polymorphed, the
creature you're changed into is female.  Whatever :-)
